From b56a469969c301c37f1553df2d5902c64bcd1af4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:23:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] Bound the whole verified read, its callback included,
 and close its client

Under authority 'verifier', verifiedRead (agreed), readAt and blockHashIs each run as ONE operation:
- one deadline settles the operation even when the caller's read callback never settles (root probe: 100 ms
  budget, still pending after 401 ms). JavaScript cannot abort the callback; it is no longer waited for and
  anything it does later is refused;
- when the operation settles (answer, refusal or deadline) it is closed: the AbortSignal handed to the
  transport is aborted (the loopback HTTP verifier cancels its fetch; an in-process verifier receives it as a
  4th argument), pending requests reject at once, the deadline timer is cleared, and a client the callback
  kept cannot send again;
- every request re-checks closure and the deadline when the transport is actually invoked, not only when it
  is queued;
- a body that outlived its deadline never moves lastBlock/lastEvidence; readAt stays history (never fresh
  authority).

Block-hash pinning, freshness, monotonicity, admin-pinned authorities, no provider fallback and the legacy
quorum path are unchanged.
